%% Figure 2 — Communication Flow Diagram
%% Sequence of a single extrusion command from URScript to stepper.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant UR as URScript<br/>(UR30)
    participant RTDE as RTDE server<br/>(port 30004)
    participant B as Bridge daemon<br/>(Python, 125 Hz)
    participant K as Klipper host<br/>(klippy)
    participant F as Klipper MCU<br/>(RP2040)
    participant M as Stepper<br/>motor

    UR->>RTDE: write output_int_register_0<br/>(mode=1) + rate + enable
    loop every 8 ms (125 Hz)
        B->>RTDE: read output registers
        Note over B: state machine +<br/>extrusion profile +<br/>MAX_RATE clamp
        B->>K: MANUAL_STEPPER MOVE=… VELOCITY=…
        K->>F: binary step schedule<br/>(USB 12 Mbps)
        F->>M: STEP / DIR / EN pulses
        F-->>K: status report
        K-->>B: tmc_status / position
        B->>RTDE: write input registers<br/>(status, actual_rate, ready, fault)
    end
    Note over B,F: Watchdog: if no RTDE packet<br/>for 500 ms → disable stepper<br/>→ write fault=1 to UR
